WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.063
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:42.333 --> 00:48.000
LAS PALMAS DE GRAN CANARIA, CANARY ISLANDS - DAY 1

3
01:44.750 --> 01:46.833
Evacuate the area immediately.

4
01:49.083 --> 01:52.750
For security reasons and due to a state of emergency,

5
01:52.833 --> 01:55.916
access is restricted until further notice.

6
01:57.250 --> 02:00.291
Please, move. Move, quickly.

7
02:01.083 --> 02:03.916
All right, let's go, sir. Pack it up, please.

8
02:09.208 --> 02:12.250
We repeat, please evacuate the beach immediately

9
02:12.375 --> 02:15.000
Let's hope you and your family get infected!!

10
02:15.083 --> 02:17.083
Your father is a murderer

11
02:21.250 --> 02:23.166
DAD

12
02:26.916 --> 02:28.250
- What happened? - Roberto?

13
02:28.333 --> 02:30.500
- Roberto, can you hear me? - Yes. What's going on?

14
02:30.583 --> 02:32.958
Don't listen to them, get to the airport now.

15
02:33.041 --> 02:36.416
- The government is closing the airspace. - Tell him to get on the plane now.

16
02:36.500 --> 02:37.583
Are you okay?

17
02:37.666 --> 02:40.125
We got you a seat on a private flight to Zaragoza,

18
02:40.208 --> 02:42.375
but you have to hurry. Do you understand?

19
02:43.083 --> 02:45.458
Okay. I'm on my way.

20
02:57.833 --> 03:00.250
SPRING 2025

21
03:00.333 --> 03:03.625
A VIRUS OF UNKNOWN ORIGIN, TSJ, SPREADS ACROSS THE GLOBE

22
03:05.083 --> 03:08.500
Massive outbreaks of TSJ have been detected, causing a collapse...

23
03:08.583 --> 03:11.208
...as well as incidents like the one at Vigo Airport...

24
03:11.291 --> 03:13.333
...wounds and bites continue to cause...

25
03:13.416 --> 03:17.875
Lockdown is being extended for cities with more than 400,000 inhabitants.

26
03:17.958 --> 03:21.375
All remaining populated areas will be moved to secure locations.

27
03:21.458 --> 03:23.791
CONTAINMENT MEASURES PROVE INSUFFICIENT

28
03:27.541 --> 03:31.000
The spread of TSJ is out of control worldwide.

29
03:31.916 --> 03:34.250
THE CANARY ISLANDS BECOME EUROPE'S FINAL REFUGE

30
03:34.333 --> 03:37.041
THOUSANDS OF SURVIVORS ARRIVE ON THE ARCHIPELAGO DAILY

31
03:37.125 --> 03:40.583
The Spanish government has relocated to the Canary Islands.

32
03:40.666 --> 03:43.083
From La Graciosa, the president hopes to monitor

33
03:43.166 --> 03:45.250
any new outbreaks emerging on the mainland.

34
03:46.416 --> 03:49.958
QUARANTINE FAILS ON THE ISLANDS OF LA GRACIOSA AND LANZAROTE

35
03:50.041 --> 03:52.333
THE GOVERNMENT TAKES DRASTIC MEASURES

36
03:56.458 --> 03:58.166
Twenty, one, three.

37
04:01.375 --> 04:03.833
RESOURCES ARE STRAINED ON THE REST OF THE ARCHIPELAGO

38
04:03.916 --> 04:07.291
Antibiotics and vaccine stocks are nearly depleted.

39
04:07.375 --> 04:09.583
...a national rationing system for basic resources.

40
04:09.666 --> 04:13.583
Each citizen will receive a ration card to record their...

41
04:13.666 --> 04:16.375
TO MAINTAIN ORDER AND TO CONTROL THE FLOW OF MIGRATION

42
04:16.458 --> 04:18.375
THE CIVILIAN POPULATION IS MILITARIZED

43
04:18.458 --> 04:22.000
All citizens must report to registration and training centers...

44
04:22.083 --> 04:23.083
RECRUITMENT

45
04:23.166 --> 04:26.208
...and comply with the orders of military and civil authorities.

46
04:26.291 --> 04:29.791
Those who resist will face criminal penalties

47
04:29.875 --> 04:31.708
once normalcy is reestablished.

48
04:32.416 --> 04:37.541
APOCALYPSE Z: NEW WORLD

49
04:38.208 --> 04:39.833
SENTRY POINT 3 NORTH

50
04:39.916 --> 04:42.583
LAS PALMAS, CANARY ISLANDS

51
04:42.666 --> 04:45.166
6 MONTHS LATER

52
05:13.666 --> 05:17.583
Contact detected 15 nautical miles from this position

53
05:17.666 --> 05:22.583
at coordinates 28o10'N, 16o20'W.

54
05:22.666 --> 05:24.500
Come on, come on, let's go.

55
05:24.583 --> 05:26.708
This isn't a walk in the park, damn it.

56
05:29.833 --> 05:32.000
Sentry to base. We have contact.

57
05:32.083 --> 05:34.625
This is the Spanish Army.

58
05:34.708 --> 05:38.291
Cut your engines and prepare to be boarded.

59
05:39.166 --> 05:44.875
I repeat, cut your engines and prepare to be boarded.

60
05:53.750 --> 05:57.583
Remain on deck. We're going to check your condition.

61
05:57.666 --> 05:59.416
We've come from Cádiz, from Sanlúcar.

62
05:59.500 --> 06:02.791
- Is anyone else on board? - No. Just me and my husband.

63
06:02.875 --> 06:05.500
- Are you sure? - We're sure. We don't have any symptoms.

64
06:05.583 --> 06:06.500
I swear.

65
06:06.583 --> 06:08.375
Martínez, Rincón, take their temperature.

66
06:08.458 --> 06:09.833
Román, Park, check the cabin.

67
06:09.916 --> 06:12.708
Don't move, ma'am. Don't move.

68
06:16.416 --> 06:18.250
Move back. Stand back.

69
06:22.583 --> 06:23.750
Start with her.

70
06:25.625 --> 06:27.708
We just want to get to the Canaries, I swear.

71
06:27.791 --> 06:30.791
We're going to do a routine safety inspection.

72
06:30.875 --> 06:34.208
Before disembarking, it will be mandatory to go through quarantine.

73
06:37.250 --> 06:38.833
And how long does that last?

74
06:38.916 --> 06:41.583
It depends. But don't worry, you'll be kept informed.

75
07:33.916 --> 07:35.000
What are you doing?

76
07:35.083 --> 07:36.500
Don't fuck me over, Tae.

77
07:36.583 --> 07:38.000
You'll get us in trouble.

78
07:38.083 --> 07:40.666
Do you want to be a loser the rest of your life?

79
07:45.875 --> 07:47.416
I'm not like that, man.

80
07:51.875 --> 07:54.833
- What's going on? - Please, don't make this any harder.

81
08:24.833 --> 08:28.166
- When did you leave the mainland? - About a week ago.

82
09:06.083 --> 09:07.250
Infected!

83
09:07.333 --> 09:10.333
No! Please, no.

84
09:10.416 --> 09:11.625
No! Don't hurt him!

85
09:11.708 --> 09:13.916
What the fuck are you doing out there? Idiot!

86
09:18.541 --> 09:19.583
Please, no!

87
09:19.666 --> 09:21.500
I'm okay.

88
09:23.208 --> 09:25.083
Don't hurt my son!

89
09:25.166 --> 09:28.250
- I'm okay. - He's going to be fine! Please!

90
09:28.333 --> 09:29.583
- I'm okay. - Please!

91
09:32.041 --> 09:33.000
No!

92
09:38.250 --> 09:42.708
QUARANTINE

93
09:42.791 --> 09:44.083
Here you go.

94
09:53.500 --> 09:54.666
Private Park,

95
09:54.750 --> 09:58.875
your superior informed us that you abandoned your post

96
09:58.958 --> 10:01.791
and failed to notice the presence of an infected person.

97
10:01.875 --> 10:03.541
- Is that correct? - Yes, sir.

98
10:03.625 --> 10:06.958
I hope you realize how serious these accusations are.

99
10:08.583 --> 10:11.458
Okay, then it's my duty to inform you that you're under arrest

100
10:11.541 --> 10:14.083
for abandoning your post and endangering a fellow soldier.

101
10:16.000 --> 10:18.625
If you have anything else to say, please say it now,

102
10:18.708 --> 10:20.875
so it can be included in your arrest record.

103
10:24.750 --> 10:25.666
Okay?

104
10:59.208 --> 11:00.625
Adopt him already, man.

105
11:01.958 --> 11:04.041
I've told you a thousand times, I can't.

106
11:04.875 --> 11:06.333
I don't have the space.

107
11:07.208 --> 11:10.333
He hasn't gotten close to anyone since Manel died.

108
11:11.041 --> 11:12.125
No one.

109
11:18.625 --> 11:21.541
Take whatever you want from that box. I'll take everything.

110
11:38.291 --> 11:40.708
This? For those rings?

111
11:42.083 --> 11:43.458
Damn, man.

112
11:50.750 --> 11:54.666
If you want to improve your situation, we can talk.

113
11:55.250 --> 11:57.708
They want to send a mission to Madrid.

114
11:57.791 --> 12:00.291
Operation Ithaca. Heard of it?

115
12:01.375 --> 12:05.041
They want to bring supplies to the islands,

116
12:05.125 --> 12:09.250
and what I want is to place someone in Inventory,

117
12:09.333 --> 12:11.916
to help me divert certain merchandise.

118
12:13.541 --> 12:15.625
You want to send someone to the mainland?

119
12:16.208 --> 12:18.500
- To hustle? - Anxiety meds.

120
12:19.791 --> 12:21.833
They're worth more than diamonds now.

121
12:24.416 --> 12:25.583
Roberto...

122
12:28.416 --> 12:30.500
The Canaries are really fucked.

123
12:31.666 --> 12:35.041
We're not gonna last another month. At least not like this.

124
12:35.958 --> 12:38.541
Why do you sound like all those pessimists?

125
12:38.625 --> 12:40.500
The government can't hold on anymore.

126
12:41.250 --> 12:42.750
The opposition can't either.

127
12:42.833 --> 12:45.166
They're just waiting to see who shoots first,

128
12:45.250 --> 12:46.916
and when that happens,

129
12:47.000 --> 12:51.083
we won't need the infected to put us through hell here.

130
12:54.208 --> 12:56.666
What do you say? Feel like going to Madrid?

131
12:58.666 --> 13:00.000
No fucking way.

132
13:07.958 --> 13:09.083
And I'm taking this.

133
13:36.125 --> 13:37.791
MISSING

134
13:46.958 --> 13:50.625
Enough with the waves of migrants coming here to eat your food,

135
13:50.708 --> 13:54.666
overwhelm your hospitals and infect you.

136
13:54.750 --> 13:56.750
Enough! It's over!

137
13:58.166 --> 14:00.125
We must never forget...

138
14:00.208 --> 14:01.500
FOOD BANK YOUR HELP FEEDS HOPE

139
14:01.583 --> 14:03.041
...what went wrong on La Graciosa.

140
14:03.125 --> 14:05.250
The time has come to demand a government

141
14:05.333 --> 14:09.208
that doesn't lie to you, that tells the truth.

142
14:09.291 --> 14:12.541
A new government with the courage to close the borders!

143
14:12.625 --> 14:14.166
DEMONSTRATION TOMORROW IN LAS PALMAS

144
14:14.250 --> 14:17.458
Those were the words of opposition leader González-Escalona.

145
14:38.125 --> 14:40.083
- What's up? - What's up, Moncho?

146
14:45.458 --> 14:47.166
Hey, how was the rotation?

147
14:48.041 --> 14:50.458
Two weeks wasted, for a change.

148
14:50.541 --> 14:53.875
They cut our intranet here. We were without cellphones for a few days.

149
14:53.958 --> 14:55.625
You didn't miss much either.

150
14:56.208 --> 14:58.583
They got the water treatment plant back up.

151
14:58.666 --> 15:01.250
Now you can shower for more than a minute at a time.

152
15:02.416 --> 15:03.500
Shit.

153
15:03.583 --> 15:07.125
Hope someone does something and shakes the fucking government up.

154
15:08.041 --> 15:09.458
Good luck with that.

155
15:11.583 --> 15:13.958
Hey, are you going to the demonstration?

156
15:16.125 --> 15:17.791
No, and neither should you.

157
15:17.875 --> 15:19.916
You're gassing up a madman.

158
15:20.416 --> 15:21.833
A madman, he says.

159
15:21.916 --> 15:25.666
Escalona is the only one who's doing anything to change things.

160
15:31.833 --> 15:33.500
Something's going down. Let's go!

161
15:34.500 --> 15:35.541
Hurry!

162
15:35.625 --> 15:36.583
Fight!

163
15:36.666 --> 15:37.625
Come on!

164
15:50.375 --> 15:52.666
- Leave me alone, man. - Where are you going?

165
15:52.750 --> 15:55.541
You can't go up there. I'm not gonna tell you again.

166
15:55.625 --> 15:57.916
I know you almost got a soldier killed.

167
15:58.000 --> 15:59.083
Get out of here!

168
15:59.166 --> 16:01.666
Please, I just want to go home, okay?

169
16:01.750 --> 16:03.583
This isn't your home, buddy.

170
16:03.666 --> 16:05.375
Go on, get out of here.

171
16:06.458 --> 16:08.833
- Don't you understand Spanish? - I am Spanish.

172
16:08.916 --> 16:10.333
- Hey! - Watch out.

173
16:10.416 --> 16:12.125
Let's see if you understand that.

174
16:12.208 --> 16:13.291
And who are you?

175
16:13.375 --> 16:14.250
Let him through.

176
16:14.333 --> 16:16.541
You can't even see with those eyes.

177
16:16.625 --> 16:17.916
Leave it. Hey.

178
16:19.916 --> 16:22.125
This dumbass left his fellow soldier hanging.

179
16:22.208 --> 16:23.541
That soldier was me. I'm fine.

180
16:23.625 --> 16:24.833
- Okay? Yes. - Yeah? Okay.

181
16:24.916 --> 16:26.416
Let us by, please.

182
16:26.500 --> 16:28.041
What? Are you butt buddies?

183
16:57.041 --> 16:58.666
With your permission, Captain.

184
17:06.916 --> 17:09.583
I should have guessed you were the one fighting.

185
17:10.166 --> 17:11.208
How are you?

186
17:16.166 --> 17:18.083
Better than the other guy, it seems.

187
17:21.166 --> 17:24.250
I wouldn't brag about breaking a superior's back.

188
17:26.541 --> 17:27.500
A superior?

189
17:27.583 --> 17:28.791
A sergeant.

190
17:31.833 --> 17:35.833
- You have to take this seriously... - Forgive me, Marina...

191
17:36.500 --> 17:40.833
but I don't need another one of your lectures.

192
17:41.416 --> 17:44.333
Okay? You're not my instructor anymore.

193
17:48.666 --> 17:49.916
I'm still your superior.

194
17:54.500 --> 17:57.375
Roberto Román? Come with me.

195
18:17.166 --> 18:18.250
Thank God.

196
18:18.333 --> 18:19.958
You got my message.

197
18:22.291 --> 18:24.375
The commander owes me a few favors,

198
18:24.458 --> 18:26.791
but I won't be able to stay long.

199
18:26.875 --> 18:29.000
Tell them to let me out of here, please.

200
18:29.083 --> 18:31.458
I'm tired of explaining that it was an accident.

201
18:31.541 --> 18:32.916
Accident or not,

202
18:33.000 --> 18:35.625
the Madrid mission is now short a sergeant.

203
18:35.708 --> 18:38.000
- Because of you. - Well, he deserved it.

204
18:38.083 --> 18:39.458
That doesn't matter.

205
18:40.041 --> 18:43.291
He's a sergeant, you're only a conscript.

206
18:43.375 --> 18:45.250
Hey, talk to someone, please.

207
18:45.333 --> 18:47.041
You're well-connected.

208
18:47.125 --> 18:49.541
You must know someone who can resolve all this.

209
18:49.625 --> 18:51.666
- It was an accident. - You don't understand.

210
18:51.750 --> 18:53.541
I can't help you this time.

211
18:55.916 --> 18:57.583
The judge knows who you are.

212
18:59.583 --> 19:01.875
She knows your father is Enrique Román,

213
19:01.958 --> 19:05.541
and she's not going to let off the son of the man who ignored protocols

214
19:05.625 --> 19:08.583
and caused the first mass infection in Spain.

215
19:09.666 --> 19:11.583
What does my father have to do with this?

216
19:11.666 --> 19:13.458
I don't even know where he is.

217
19:13.541 --> 19:15.083
That doesn't matter.

218
19:15.166 --> 19:17.500
People are lashing out at politicians,

219
19:17.583 --> 19:19.708
and you're the closest thing they have.

220
19:19.791 --> 19:22.166
Prit, I'm nobody.

221
19:22.250 --> 19:23.250
Understand?

222
19:23.333 --> 19:25.583
And my father is a scapegoat.

223
19:25.666 --> 19:26.708
I get it.

224
19:27.958 --> 19:31.208
But the justice system that used to protect you

225
19:31.291 --> 19:33.958
is now using you as an example. That's how it is now.

226
19:34.041 --> 19:35.458
You have to help me.

227
19:36.875 --> 19:38.125
And you can do it.

228
19:41.208 --> 19:42.625
There's one option.

229
19:43.708 --> 19:45.208
The Madrid operation.

230
19:46.083 --> 19:49.500
They still need people in Inventory.

231
19:49.583 --> 19:51.875
I can pull a few strings.

232
19:52.916 --> 19:54.666
I help you get out of here,

233
19:55.375 --> 19:58.750
you help me divert merchandise there.

234
19:58.833 --> 20:00.875
That's the only thing I can think of.

235
20:00.958 --> 20:02.916
It's better than sitting in jail.

236
20:03.708 --> 20:04.750
Really?

237
20:04.833 --> 20:07.416
At least there you'll have guns to defend yourself.

238
20:07.500 --> 20:11.000
You won't last a day here in prison, believe me.

239
20:15.000 --> 20:18.208
LAS PALMAS AIR BASE, GRAND CANARY ISLAND

240
20:48.625 --> 20:49.958
On your feet!

241
20:52.750 --> 20:54.291
Awaiting orders, Major.

242
21:02.583 --> 21:03.666
At ease.

243
21:05.166 --> 21:07.125
Ladies, gentlemen,

244
21:07.208 --> 21:09.208
I am Major Joaquín De Luna.

245
21:09.833 --> 21:13.583
To my left, Captain Parra. To my right, Captain Castro.

246
21:14.291 --> 21:17.875
In a few hours, all of you will depart for Cuatro Vientos,

247
21:17.958 --> 21:19.916
the airfield where the government stockpiled

248
21:20.000 --> 21:22.250
most of their resources before evacuating Madrid.

249
21:22.333 --> 21:23.250
OPERATION ITHACA

250
21:23.333 --> 21:27.583
The mission is to obtain supplies and create a route for the transit of goods

251
21:27.666 --> 21:29.708
from the mainland to the archipelago.

252
21:29.791 --> 21:32.791
For this, two tactical subgroups have been formed.

253
21:32.875 --> 21:34.750
The first, led by Captain Parra,

254
21:34.833 --> 21:36.833
will act as a covering force

255
21:36.916 --> 21:40.250
and will deploy first once we have landed.

256
21:40.333 --> 21:43.708
Afterward, they will head toward the buildings in the north sector.

257
21:43.791 --> 21:46.041
The second will be led by Captain Castro

258
21:46.125 --> 21:49.375
and will occupy the buildings at the rear of the complex.

259
21:49.458 --> 21:51.875
We'll travel light, but secure.

260
21:51.958 --> 21:55.291
Protective mesh under your uniform and as much ammunition as possible.

261
21:55.375 --> 21:57.000
Keep in mind that we will move fast.

262
21:57.083 --> 22:00.041
Although resistance may be limited, we can't count on that.

263
22:01.250 --> 22:04.541
At this point, the probability of finding survivors in Madrid

264
22:04.625 --> 22:05.708
is virtually zero,

265
22:05.791 --> 22:07.333
but if it does happen,

266
22:07.416 --> 22:11.166
you must avoid all contact with anyone outside the mission.

267
22:11.250 --> 22:14.666
For now, we don't have the capacity to organize rescues.

268
22:14.750 --> 22:18.083
We can't rescue anyone because we can't rescue everyone.

269
22:18.166 --> 22:20.541
That is not our responsibility.

270
22:20.625 --> 22:23.625
Now you will receive instructions on health precautions

271
22:23.708 --> 22:26.666
from Lucía Iglesias, our Medical Director.

272
22:26.750 --> 22:30.250
She has survived much longer in the trenches than any of us.

273
22:31.208 --> 22:32.208
Come on up.

274
22:43.750 --> 22:44.625
Ignacio.

275
22:45.458 --> 22:47.208
- Roberto. - What's up?

276
22:48.375 --> 22:50.500
I'm the Signal Specialist.

277
22:51.000 --> 22:52.208
They call me Core.

278
22:52.291 --> 22:55.875
Or "Core Dump," or "The Processor," or just "The IT Guy."

279
22:55.958 --> 22:58.625
Fucking disgusting. This thing is full of conscripts.

280
23:00.958 --> 23:03.666
Hey! This is a really good squad.

281
23:04.500 --> 23:07.166
They held on for hours and hours on the Mali coast.

282
23:07.750 --> 23:09.458
You won't have any trouble.

283
23:10.458 --> 23:11.916
- Manuel. - What is it?

284
23:12.000 --> 23:13.333
Guzmán.

285
23:14.041 --> 23:15.833
He doesn't much like conscripts.

286
23:15.916 --> 23:18.666
Doesn't like to get attached in case he has to kill them later.

287
23:18.750 --> 23:20.375
Hey, girl. What's up, recruit?

288
23:20.458 --> 23:23.583
So nice of them to take us on a field trip.

289
23:25.125 --> 23:26.250
Comillas.

290
23:26.333 --> 23:29.000
They call her that for the neighborhood in Madrid, not the...

291
23:29.833 --> 23:31.500
You're the new Notary, right?

292
23:32.083 --> 23:33.916
That's what they call the logistics guy.

293
23:34.000 --> 23:36.583
The last guy debuted and retired on the same day.

294
23:36.666 --> 23:39.750
So I hope that in addition to organizing supplies,

295
23:39.833 --> 23:41.500
you also know how to shoot.

296
23:53.541 --> 23:55.458
Let's go.

297
23:55.541 --> 23:58.083
On three. One, two, three.

298
23:58.166 --> 23:59.458
Delta!

299
23:59.541 --> 24:00.875
One, two, three.

300
24:00.958 --> 24:01.958
Delta!

301
24:02.041 --> 24:03.875
One, two, three.

302
24:03.958 --> 24:04.875
Delta!

303
24:32.125 --> 24:34.000
Eagle 1 to Madrid Control.

304
24:34.625 --> 24:36.666
...entering the mainland sector.

305
24:37.708 --> 24:41.291
Initiating mainland overflight. Flight level 204.

306
24:41.375 --> 24:43.833
Clear sky. Good visibility at ten kilometers.

307
24:43.916 --> 24:46.041
Light wind from the northeast, no turbulence.

308
25:01.291 --> 25:03.416
I don't want to know how they let you come.

309
25:05.000 --> 25:09.208
But this squad has been functioning like a family for weeks.

310
25:09.291 --> 25:10.833
You better be up to the task.

311
25:13.583 --> 25:16.333
Keep your eyes open. Understood?

312
25:18.708 --> 25:20.583
- Yes. - "Yes, Sergeant."

313
25:21.541 --> 25:22.750
Yes, Sergeant.

314
25:31.916 --> 25:33.416
You've got a thing for her.

315
25:41.583 --> 25:44.166
Initiating reconnaissance flight over the city.

316
25:44.250 --> 25:45.416
Separation in progress.

317
26:15.500 --> 26:16.625
Five minutes!

318
26:16.708 --> 26:18.250
Five minutes.

319
26:46.291 --> 26:49.291
Landing complete. On the ground.

320
26:50.416 --> 26:51.958
Falcon to Chimneysweep.

321
26:52.041 --> 26:53.666
Initiating deployment.

322
26:53.750 --> 26:56.625
Roger that. From now on, radio silence.

323
26:56.708 --> 26:57.625
Falcon.

324
27:02.583 --> 27:03.625
Perimeter defense.

325
27:03.708 --> 27:05.250
Sharpshooters on their way.

326
27:05.750 --> 27:07.625
Remember, with the ammunition we use,

327
27:07.708 --> 27:10.041
it's best to shoot for the head, not the chest.

328
27:10.125 --> 27:12.583
A shot between the eyes is best.

329
27:12.666 --> 27:14.250
- Ready? - Yes, Sergeant!

330
27:40.958 --> 27:42.708
Falcon to Chimneysweep. All clear.

331
27:55.708 --> 27:57.000
Welcome to Madrid.

332
28:15.416 --> 28:18.958
Core to all. Launching reconnaissance drone.

333
28:27.083 --> 28:30.916
Chimneysweep to all. Delta moving on objective.

334
28:31.000 --> 28:34.083
Falcon says Alpha is inspecting the perimeter.

335
28:34.791 --> 28:35.625
Infected!

336
28:39.625 --> 28:40.791
On alert!

337
28:47.041 --> 28:49.208
Chimneysweep to Core. Status report.

338
28:49.291 --> 28:50.416
All clear.

339
28:51.500 --> 28:54.875
Finger off the trigger, asshole. You want to get us all killed?

340
29:20.000 --> 29:22.125
Chimneysweep to Falcon. All in order?

341
29:22.958 --> 29:25.333
No activity inside the perimeter buildings.

342
29:25.416 --> 29:27.583
We're almost at the target.

343
29:27.666 --> 29:28.708
Advancing.

344
30:05.708 --> 30:08.250
Wanna let them get a little closer, asshole?

345
30:09.250 --> 30:12.458
Chimneysweep to Core. There must be more. Do you have visual contact?

346
30:12.541 --> 30:13.791
Checking.

347
30:26.333 --> 30:29.333
Group of 30 located on your left flank, 300 meters.

348
30:29.416 --> 30:30.833
What we were expecting.

349
30:42.416 --> 30:43.625
Falcon to Chimneysweep.

350
30:43.708 --> 30:46.041
Infected coming out of the metro stations.

351
30:46.125 --> 30:48.541
I repeat, infected coming out of the metro stations.

352
30:48.625 --> 30:49.583
Maintain position!

353
30:49.666 --> 30:51.958
The stations are outside the perimeter.

354
30:52.041 --> 30:54.166
Only a limited number can get in.

355
31:05.291 --> 31:06.208
Fire!

356
31:10.291 --> 31:12.458
Come on, shoot! They aren't people!

357
31:15.416 --> 31:16.583
Core to Chimneysweep.

358
31:16.666 --> 31:18.083
There are lots of openings.

359
31:18.166 --> 31:20.333
They must've broken the fence at several points.

360
31:21.791 --> 31:23.541
- Roll out! - Fuck!

361
31:48.458 --> 31:49.875
They're rushing in.

362
31:49.958 --> 31:51.875
I repeat, they're rushing in.

363
31:53.041 --> 31:55.208
There are openings all along the fence.

364
32:02.875 --> 32:05.041
Orchestra! Secure the perimeter!

365
32:05.125 --> 32:07.541
Find an elevated position to provide cover!

366
32:07.625 --> 32:08.625
Roger!

367
32:09.250 --> 32:10.958
Falcon, maintain position.

368
32:11.041 --> 32:12.750
Let's go for the ammunition.

369
32:12.833 --> 32:13.875
Take cover!

370
32:13.958 --> 32:15.958
Final magazine!

371
32:16.041 --> 32:18.083
I want that fucking door down!

372
32:22.833 --> 32:23.875
Final magazine!

373
32:28.708 --> 32:29.625
Final magazine.

374
32:43.416 --> 32:44.333
Quickly!

375
32:48.000 --> 32:49.375
Fall back!

376
33:14.500 --> 33:15.500
Run!

377
33:19.166 --> 33:20.083
Hurry!

378
33:41.833 --> 33:42.875
Let's go!

379
33:58.458 --> 34:01.333
Castro, get to the top floor and open fire.

380
34:01.416 --> 34:03.458
You four, with me. To the ammunition.

381
34:03.541 --> 34:04.625
Comillas, with me.

382
34:38.000 --> 34:39.041
Clear!

383
34:46.625 --> 34:48.291
Román, Cedeño, with me.

384
34:58.625 --> 35:00.666
Load up and take everything upstairs.

385
35:02.041 --> 35:04.166
ARMORY NO UNAUTHORIZED ENTRY

386
35:39.083 --> 35:41.208
Come on, come on, quickly, hurry!

387
35:51.166 --> 35:52.625
Infected!

388
35:53.250 --> 35:55.333
Cover the door.

389
36:18.541 --> 36:19.500
Out of ammo!

390
36:30.291 --> 36:32.500
Fuck! Out of ammo!

391
36:32.583 --> 36:33.750
Let's get out of here!

392
36:53.791 --> 36:54.958
Door!

393
37:03.333 --> 37:05.750
Chimneysweep to all. Do you read me?

394
37:05.833 --> 37:08.125
Loud and clear. We're on the second floor.

395
37:08.208 --> 37:09.500
Status report.

396
37:09.583 --> 37:11.708
We're dug in, almost out of ammo.

397
37:11.791 --> 37:12.916
How long will it take?

398
37:13.000 --> 37:14.458
We're working on it.

399
37:17.125 --> 37:18.083
Shit.

400
37:18.791 --> 37:19.833
The roof.

401
37:19.916 --> 37:21.541
We have to blow the roof off.

402
37:22.250 --> 37:23.125
Seriously.

403
37:23.208 --> 37:26.083
The library is up there. I saw it on the maps.

404
37:26.583 --> 37:28.083
The Notary is right.

405
37:28.166 --> 37:30.291
Let's blow the roof off!

406
38:16.750 --> 38:18.541
Charge is set and ready to go.

407
38:19.791 --> 38:20.666
Fire in the hole!

408
38:24.958 --> 38:26.958
Hurry! Bring up the ammo!

409
38:27.041 --> 38:29.041
Let's get the hell out of here!

410
38:46.750 --> 38:49.583
Keep sending up ammo! That's an order!

411
39:04.708 --> 39:06.583
No!

412
39:15.416 --> 39:17.375
Prioritize the mission!

413
40:17.541 --> 40:20.125
Get up there! Quickly!

414
40:31.875 --> 40:33.083
Get up there!

415
40:33.166 --> 40:34.666
That's an order!

416
41:13.708 --> 41:15.416
This is Orchestra to all.

417
41:16.083 --> 41:17.625
The major has fallen.

418
41:17.708 --> 41:20.416
Do you read? Major De Luna has fallen.

419
41:22.208 --> 41:25.208
Falcon, let's give them cover from here.

420
41:25.291 --> 41:27.541
Prepare to repair the perimeter.

421
41:29.541 --> 41:30.875
Notary, hey.

422
41:30.958 --> 41:33.958
That was fucking amazing, okay? Good job.

423
41:58.000 --> 41:59.541
More ammo here!

424
42:23.708 --> 42:26.333
Perimeter secured. Good work, folks.

425
43:15.666 --> 43:16.791
Román!

426
43:17.750 --> 43:18.583
Notary!

427
43:28.041 --> 43:30.583
I'm in command of the operation. You come with us.

428
43:30.666 --> 43:32.041
We've lost two notaries.

429
43:32.125 --> 43:35.375
Get ready to sweat, kid, because you're pulling double duty.

430
43:36.125 --> 43:38.375
Don't let up. You're doing fucking great.

431
43:38.458 --> 43:40.708
I asked for two assistants to help you. Over here.

432
43:41.125 --> 43:42.000
Ready?

433
43:42.625 --> 43:44.041
Manuel, go ahead.

434
43:50.041 --> 43:50.916
Are you ready?

435
43:56.208 --> 43:57.833
Charge ready to blow.

436
43:58.416 --> 43:59.250
Fire.

437
43:59.750 --> 44:01.041
Fire in the hole!

438
44:19.500 --> 44:20.541
Clear!

439
44:29.875 --> 44:33.708
SUPPLY BUILDING NORTH SECTOR, SECTION B

440
44:53.333 --> 44:54.708
People have been looting.

441
44:55.541 --> 44:57.458
Must've gotten in through the windows.

442
44:58.041 --> 44:59.375
Poor things.

443
45:01.416 --> 45:03.750
How many survivors are left in the area?

444
45:03.833 --> 45:05.458
You didn't notice from the plane?

445
45:05.541 --> 45:08.750
I don't think anyone is still alive in this fucking city.

446
45:08.833 --> 45:11.541
Save the chit-chat for when we're home, okay?

447
45:11.625 --> 45:13.500
- Yes, Captain. - Yes, Captain.

448
45:13.583 --> 45:16.000
We'll split up. In pairs.

449
45:16.083 --> 45:18.166
Guzmán, Comillas, with me.

450
45:18.250 --> 45:20.291
Manuel, Core, upstairs.

451
45:20.375 --> 45:22.125
Marina and Roberto, boxes.

452
45:22.208 --> 45:23.083
Let's go.

453
45:24.125 --> 45:26.708
She's the best option to replace the major.

454
45:27.208 --> 45:28.791
Have you known her long?

455
45:29.291 --> 45:31.125
Since she got back from La Graciosa.

456
45:31.750 --> 45:33.000
Her daughter died there.

457
45:35.041 --> 45:37.041
That's why she doesn't tolerate distraction.

458
45:38.625 --> 45:40.375
That was a nightmare.

459
45:40.875 --> 45:44.083
What the infected didn't kill, the bombings did.

460
45:55.875 --> 45:57.083
Opera to Orchestra.

461
45:57.166 --> 45:59.291
There's been some minor thefts from the pharmacy,

462
45:59.375 --> 46:00.833
but nothing significant.

463
46:12.750 --> 46:13.875
Do you have any family?

464
46:15.791 --> 46:17.083
A sister.

465
46:17.833 --> 46:18.916
Herminia.

466
46:19.416 --> 46:20.916
She's my twin sister.

467
46:22.291 --> 46:24.958
She was with her boyfriend in a place like this,

468
46:25.041 --> 46:27.416
but never evacuated to the Canaries.

469
46:28.000 --> 46:30.375
I still have hope that they're alive.

470
46:32.333 --> 46:35.250
Although every day it gets harder to believe, to be honest.

471
46:35.333 --> 46:36.291
Don't give up.

472
46:39.708 --> 46:41.333
It's all we have left.

473
46:46.333 --> 46:47.583
Opera to Orchestra.

474
46:47.666 --> 46:50.958
Inquiring about the estimated time of arrival for support.

475
46:51.041 --> 46:52.625
Orchestra to Opera.

476
46:52.708 --> 46:55.958
Estimated arrival for support, 30 minutes.

477
46:56.041 --> 46:57.791
Continue with the assigned procedure.

478
46:58.375 --> 46:59.250
Opera.

479
47:11.791 --> 47:13.166
Comillas to all.

480
47:13.250 --> 47:16.583
Want some wetsuits? I just found a whole box.

481
47:17.291 --> 47:19.458
Where are you? I've lost sight of you.

482
47:19.541 --> 47:22.041
Near the pharmacy, doing some shopping.

483
47:22.125 --> 47:23.333
On my way.

484
47:23.416 --> 47:26.291
This is Nightingale. If you find a game console, let me know.

485
47:46.500 --> 47:49.083
Look at him. With his finger in the right place.

486
47:49.166 --> 47:51.791
I don't think I have to give you any more lessons.

487
47:51.875 --> 47:52.958
Leave him alone.

488
47:53.833 --> 47:56.208
I don't think you'd have done better on your first day.

489
48:07.583 --> 48:10.416
This is Core. Come up and see this, please.

490
48:11.125 --> 48:12.250
Come on, Román.

491
48:21.666 --> 48:23.250
- Are you okay? - Yeah.

492
48:24.291 --> 48:26.500
Check out the relics Core found.

493
48:31.666 --> 48:32.916
It doesn't make sense.

494
48:33.000 --> 48:35.625
Either this airport hasn't been updated since Y2K,

495
48:35.708 --> 48:37.166
or something's very weird.

496
48:37.250 --> 48:38.458
Opera to Pottymouth.

497
48:38.541 --> 48:40.791
Requesting assistance opening the garage door.

498
48:40.875 --> 48:42.083
Let's see if it starts up.

499
48:56.166 --> 48:58.833
No way. You've gotta be kidding me.

500
49:03.791 --> 49:04.708
What is it?

501
49:05.375 --> 49:06.541
The Internet works.

502
49:06.625 --> 49:09.666
- What? - Yeah, the Internet works.

503
49:11.791 --> 49:13.541
There are so many destroyed hubs

504
49:13.625 --> 49:16.166
because the bandwidth must have been reduced.

505
49:17.416 --> 49:19.458
Telnet. Gopher.

506
49:20.083 --> 49:22.875
It's like the Internet from 40 years ago, but it works.

507
49:22.958 --> 49:25.500
But that's impossible, Core. There's no electricity.

508
49:26.208 --> 49:27.333
Yes, there is.

509
49:27.416 --> 49:29.500
The phone line has its own current.

510
49:31.916 --> 49:35.416
Does that mean there's a working telephone switchboard?

511
49:35.500 --> 49:37.916
It's likely, but surely it's autonomous.

512
49:43.291 --> 49:44.875
Look, these are chats.

513
49:52.208 --> 49:54.000
Is there anybody from Madrid?

514
49:55.041 --> 49:56.333
Madrid - HELP

515
49:58.166 --> 49:59.791
Elias - Activity detected in Madrid

516
50:02.333 --> 50:05.458
Elias - Hello You - Hello!!

517
50:10.250 --> 50:11.458
Elias - I'm a bot.

518
50:11.541 --> 50:14.791
This message posts automatically when activity is detected on this channel.

519
50:15.250 --> 50:16.541
Last response: 2 months ago

520
50:16.625 --> 50:19.750
"There is no one to care for my soul." Psalms 142:4

521
50:22.750 --> 50:23.833
Core.

522
50:25.791 --> 50:26.791
Core.

523
50:28.041 --> 50:30.458
Do you think we can access our emails?

524
50:32.958 --> 50:34.208
I think so, but...

525
50:35.208 --> 50:39.208
I have to connect two modems in parallel to go a little faster.

526
50:40.666 --> 50:42.000
Orchestra to Notary.

527
50:44.083 --> 50:44.958
Román...

528
50:50.500 --> 50:51.916
Orchestra to Notary.

529
50:52.000 --> 50:54.208
The assistants are here. You can get to work.

530
50:54.291 --> 50:55.583
Roger that.

531
51:13.416 --> 51:14.375
PEAS

532
51:17.250 --> 51:18.750
INSPECTED

533
51:21.583 --> 51:22.458
Maldonado.

534
52:29.750 --> 52:31.208
Careful they don't catch you.

535
52:32.250 --> 52:33.583
I'm just working.

536
52:35.750 --> 52:37.208
I know your boss.

537
52:38.291 --> 52:39.500
I know what you do for him.

538
52:40.708 --> 52:43.708
Just don't touch the important medications.

539
52:45.416 --> 52:46.875
Tell him that from me.

540
52:53.416 --> 52:55.791
This too. With the first shipment.

541
54:45.541 --> 54:46.791
Sorry.

542
54:48.416 --> 54:50.041
You can't sleep either?

543
54:53.291 --> 54:54.166
May I?

544
55:12.541 --> 55:13.958
I'm sorry about your sister.

545
55:16.666 --> 55:17.791
Thank you.

546
55:20.666 --> 55:22.166
Is your family okay?

547
55:25.166 --> 55:26.625
Yeah, I think so.

548
55:26.708 --> 55:28.500
I think they're safe.

549
55:30.250 --> 55:31.625
What I don't know is where.

550
55:32.666 --> 55:37.000
I tried to go with them when all this started,

551
55:37.083 --> 55:39.375
but as hard as my father tried,

552
55:40.791 --> 55:42.208
it was impossible.

553
55:43.708 --> 55:45.083
I'm sorry.

554
55:45.166 --> 55:47.625
No, I think it's better this way.

555
55:49.250 --> 55:52.541
After all the people who were infected because of him,

556
55:53.291 --> 55:56.916
I think there's some justice

557
55:57.000 --> 55:59.541
in his screw-up of a son not being able to escape.

558
56:03.333 --> 56:08.708
All I see is a forced conscript

559
56:08.791 --> 56:11.375
who's doing everything he can for his fellow soldiers.

560
56:17.750 --> 56:19.666
Can I confess something to you?

561
56:20.583 --> 56:22.375
Confession for confession?

562
56:22.458 --> 56:24.583
I feel guilty

563
56:24.666 --> 56:28.250
for having spent so much time

564
56:28.333 --> 56:31.416
hoping that my sister was alive.

565
56:32.166 --> 56:36.916
And now it's too late to say goodbye to her.

566
56:37.750 --> 56:40.125
And that feeling is suffocating me.

567
56:44.375 --> 56:47.250
You know what? I don't think it's too late to say goodbye to her.

568
58:09.333 --> 58:12.208
...Prosperidad neighborhood. This is Mateo.

569
58:12.291 --> 58:14.791
Prosperidad neighborhood. Can anyone hear me?

570
58:14.875 --> 58:16.750
I can hear you, Mateo. This is Laura.

571
58:16.833 --> 58:19.583
Thank God. Did you see the lights in the sky?

572
58:19.666 --> 58:21.666
- It came from Cuatro Vientos... - Survivors.

573
58:21.750 --> 58:23.291
...but it's impossible to get there.

574
58:23.375 --> 58:25.958
Maybe the people at the bullring can make contact.

575
58:26.750 --> 58:28.375
They're busy with the infected.

576
58:28.458 --> 58:30.625
Every day, they're having more trouble with them.

577
58:30.708 --> 58:32.833
I know, but we have to get there somehow.

578
58:32.916 --> 58:35.916
It's been four days since my son... How much longer he can last?

579
58:36.000 --> 58:38.041
This is Vicente, from the telephone exchange.

580
58:38.125 --> 58:39.750
I saw military planes.

581
58:39.833 --> 58:41.416
- Jesús, Lavapiés. - María, Chueca.

582
58:41.500 --> 58:44.333
This is Core at Cuatro Vientos. We've come from the Canaries.

583
58:44.416 --> 58:46.083
Thank God.

584
58:46.166 --> 58:47.708
My name is Alicia.

585
58:47.791 --> 58:50.458
We're at the bullring, near the M-30.

586
58:50.541 --> 58:54.333
A group of neighbors built this refuge for people in the area.

587
58:54.416 --> 58:56.500
But we won't be able to hold out another day.

588
58:56.583 --> 58:58.291
Our defenses are about to fall.

589
58:58.791 --> 59:00.166
Be right there, hold on.

590
59:00.250 --> 59:01.541
Alicia...

591
59:03.416 --> 59:06.958
Alicia, this is Captain Rocío Castro, of the Spanish Army.

592
59:07.041 --> 59:11.041
Listen to me. Right now we don't have the means to get to you,

593
59:11.125 --> 59:13.916
but we'll initiate rescue missions shortly,

594
59:14.000 --> 59:16.666
so, please, don't lose heart, okay?

595
59:16.875 --> 59:18.208
Don't talk to me about heart.

596
59:21.250 --> 59:24.291
You should have done this a long time ago,

597
59:24.375 --> 59:26.291
not left it up to us.

598
59:26.375 --> 59:29.500
You're just like all those politicians. You're going to abandon us.

599
59:31.958 --> 59:33.375
Alicia, do you hear me?

600
59:34.666 --> 59:35.958
Alicia?

601
59:44.625 --> 59:46.625
We have to help them, Captain.

602
59:49.083 --> 59:51.375
The mission is to secure this and take it with us.

603
59:51.458 --> 59:53.500
We don't have resources for anything more.

604
59:54.500 --> 59:57.000
But those people won't last another day.

605
59:57.083 --> 59:58.916
They just made that pretty clear.

606
01:00:01.708 --> 01:00:04.666
Guzmán, when will we start searching for survivors?

607
01:00:05.541 --> 01:00:08.125
That's scheduled for a few months from now, Captain.

608
01:00:09.708 --> 01:00:13.125
We're going to abandon them just because we're not ready?

609
01:00:14.333 --> 01:00:16.375
We can't do that.

610
01:00:16.458 --> 01:00:18.041
We'll find a way.

611
01:00:19.208 --> 01:00:23.416
Those people built a refuge for their neighbors.

612
01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:25.166
They're heroes.

613
01:00:30.416 --> 01:00:32.041
Captain, I don't think...

614
01:00:32.125 --> 01:00:34.083
I need to talk to central command.

615
01:00:36.291 --> 01:00:38.791
I'll see if I can send a message from the plane.

616
01:00:38.875 --> 01:00:39.750
Yes, ma'am.

617
01:01:13.041 --> 01:01:14.708
Attention all personnel.

618
01:01:14.791 --> 01:01:18.125
The government aircraft carrying González-Escalona has landed.

619
01:01:18.208 --> 01:01:21.041
Proceed with reception and security protocols.

620
01:01:21.125 --> 01:01:23.541
I repeat, González-Escalona on base.

621
01:01:24.125 --> 01:01:25.291
At your command, Major.

622
01:01:26.500 --> 01:01:28.166
Status report, Captain.

623
01:01:29.458 --> 01:01:30.500
Sixteen KIA,

624
01:01:30.583 --> 01:01:34.833
among them Major De Luna, Captain Barrena and Sergeant Cedeño.

625
01:01:34.916 --> 01:01:38.333
The openings in the perimeter fence were made by groups of survivors

626
01:01:38.416 --> 01:01:40.166
trying to reach the supplies.

627
01:01:40.250 --> 01:01:42.000
There are more than we thought.

628
01:01:47.625 --> 01:01:48.625
Prit?

629
01:01:50.291 --> 01:01:51.500
What are you doing here?

630
01:01:51.583 --> 01:01:53.750
We came to see you.

631
01:01:53.833 --> 01:01:54.958
We missed you.

632
01:01:57.333 --> 01:01:58.291
Tae.

633
01:01:59.291 --> 01:02:00.958
Ask if there's a mechanic available.

634
01:02:04.583 --> 01:02:05.750
Smart kid.

635
01:02:06.708 --> 01:02:07.708
Come on.

636
01:02:08.250 --> 01:02:11.958
Get ready, the new governor wants to speak with you all.

637
01:02:12.041 --> 01:02:14.333
González-Escalona is the new governor?

638
01:02:14.416 --> 01:02:17.833
The Las Palmas demonstration got out of hand.

639
01:02:17.916 --> 01:02:19.250
There were casualties.

640
01:02:19.333 --> 01:02:22.875
The government put him in charge of supplies,

641
01:02:22.958 --> 01:02:25.458
as long as he stops rabble-rousing.

642
01:02:25.541 --> 01:02:27.041
Wait.

643
01:02:27.958 --> 01:02:29.250
He's our new boss?

644
01:02:32.125 --> 01:02:33.250
Come on.

645
01:02:39.916 --> 01:02:42.166
Don't worry, I'm not going to give a speech.

646
01:02:42.250 --> 01:02:44.750
I'm not here today as a politician,

647
01:02:44.833 --> 01:02:49.750
or as a critic of the government, which is how you know me.

648
01:02:51.125 --> 01:02:53.291
I'm here as just another Spaniard...

649
01:02:55.083 --> 01:02:58.750
who unfortunately knows what sacrifice is, just like you.

650
01:02:59.583 --> 01:03:03.250
When I learned of your actions, I thought, I want to be there.

651
01:03:04.291 --> 01:03:06.250
I want to be there helping them.

652
01:03:06.333 --> 01:03:08.583
Helping them raise up Madrid.

653
01:03:08.666 --> 01:03:13.333
Because this airport doesn't just represent a supply depot anymore.

654
01:03:14.333 --> 01:03:18.583
This airport, right now, is the resistance,

655
01:03:19.250 --> 01:03:20.666
the courage...

656
01:03:20.750 --> 01:03:23.708
We're on the brink of a civil war.

657
01:03:23.791 --> 01:03:26.375
No one's playing clean now.

658
01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:30.916
These people's lives aren't a game.

659
01:03:32.625 --> 01:03:35.791
I need you to stick with me here for a while.

660
01:03:35.875 --> 01:03:37.541
Please.

661
01:03:41.833 --> 01:03:42.750
Bravo!

662
01:03:43.333 --> 01:03:46.208
Thank you! Thank you for your service!

663
01:03:46.291 --> 01:03:48.625
We need to prepare double the planes

664
01:03:48.708 --> 01:03:51.541
and three or four helicopters for travel to the mainland.

665
01:03:51.625 --> 01:03:53.791
We'll speak later. Roberto.

666
01:03:56.458 --> 01:03:57.500
You're Roberto, right?

667
01:04:01.625 --> 01:04:03.541
Sit down, I want to talk to you.

668
01:04:04.875 --> 01:04:06.000
Please.

669
01:04:12.750 --> 01:04:17.083
When the Ukrainian told me that you were Enrique Román's son,

670
01:04:17.166 --> 01:04:19.041
I couldn't believe it.

671
01:04:20.916 --> 01:04:21.875
Want one?

672
01:04:22.750 --> 01:04:23.750
No, thank you.

673
01:04:23.833 --> 01:04:25.625
- They're good. - I don't smoke.

674
01:04:25.708 --> 01:04:26.916
Me neither.

675
01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:31.500
They insist on giving them to me, but I haven't touched tobacco in ten years.

676
01:04:39.583 --> 01:04:41.958
I don't know if you know, but I owe your father a lot.

677
01:04:43.083 --> 01:04:44.041
My father?

678
01:04:45.000 --> 01:04:46.041
You know each other?

679
01:04:46.125 --> 01:04:48.625
Quique supported me a lot when I started in politics.

680
01:04:49.583 --> 01:04:50.875
He's a good man.

681
01:04:52.791 --> 01:04:55.916
The kind you don't meet very often in politics.

682
01:04:56.000 --> 01:04:58.375
And I think they've been very unfair to him.

683
01:04:59.041 --> 01:05:01.750
Outside and inside the party. Very.

684
01:05:04.166 --> 01:05:05.250
Do you know where he is?

685
01:05:06.208 --> 01:05:07.166
No.

686
01:05:08.416 --> 01:05:11.166
Although I assume he's still alive.

687
01:05:14.333 --> 01:05:17.416
Look, I'm going to take advantage

688
01:05:17.500 --> 01:05:20.541
of the fact that that Ukrainian friend of yours is a pilot.

689
01:05:21.208 --> 01:05:23.541
He can take me to see some people.

690
01:05:24.791 --> 01:05:25.958
Good people.

691
01:05:26.041 --> 01:05:28.458
Committed people.

692
01:05:28.541 --> 01:05:30.083
Roberto, do you understand me?

693
01:05:30.166 --> 01:05:32.375
People who know things.

694
01:05:33.708 --> 01:05:37.416
And I'm convinced they'll be happy to meet you personally.

695
01:05:38.416 --> 01:05:40.083
You want me to go with you?

696
01:05:40.166 --> 01:05:43.500
Don't rule out the possibility

697
01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.291
that one of them may know where your father is.

698
01:05:48.625 --> 01:05:50.083
He may even be there.

699
01:05:59.291 --> 01:06:02.041
Look, Roberto...

700
01:06:04.458 --> 01:06:06.916
This place isn't made for people like you and me.

701
01:06:08.625 --> 01:06:10.791
You weren't born to be a soldier, son.

702
01:06:12.500 --> 01:06:13.916
Or a smuggler.

703
01:06:17.250 --> 01:06:20.208
If not for Pritchenko, I don't know what would've become of me.

704
01:06:28.666 --> 01:06:29.833
Tae,

705
01:06:30.458 --> 01:06:33.083
what's happened to you since the last time I saw you?

706
01:06:37.083 --> 01:06:39.458
Guess I don't want to be a loser the rest of my life.

707
01:06:42.125 --> 01:06:43.125
Román.

708
01:06:45.958 --> 01:06:48.083
Go ahead. I'll be right there.

709
01:06:51.875 --> 01:06:53.958
- Sergeant? - They're letting us go.

710
01:06:54.041 --> 01:06:56.625
We're going to rescue the survivors from their stronghold.

711
01:06:56.708 --> 01:06:58.916
The new major didn't want to, but González-Escalona

712
01:06:59.000 --> 01:07:01.416
intervened to let us organize a volunteer mission.

713
01:07:01.833 --> 01:07:03.791
Come on, Román!

714
01:07:07.166 --> 01:07:09.333
Do you think that guy is trustworthy?

715
01:07:09.416 --> 01:07:10.708
I don't know,

716
01:07:10.791 --> 01:07:13.458
but if he allows us to help them, what does it matter?

717
01:07:15.291 --> 01:07:16.291
What's wrong?

718
01:07:17.208 --> 01:07:20.166
What's wrong is it's suicide. Don't you see?

719
01:07:22.083 --> 01:07:24.958
Roberto, they won't last another day without us.

720
01:07:25.041 --> 01:07:26.541
They need us.

721
01:07:27.500 --> 01:07:29.875
Giving them hope is the most important thing.

722
01:07:36.958 --> 01:07:38.625
- Will you come? - I don't know, Marina.

723
01:07:40.166 --> 01:07:41.333
I don't know.

724
01:07:44.250 --> 01:07:47.916
Then let's say goodbye now, okay?

725
01:07:55.916 --> 01:07:57.458
I hope it goes well for you.

726
01:08:23.458 --> 01:08:25.541
Ready. Okay.

727
01:08:31.458 --> 01:08:32.583
Pilar.

728
01:08:33.166 --> 01:08:35.000
Hey, girl.

729
01:08:36.875 --> 01:08:38.333
Captain Castro.

730
01:08:43.000 --> 01:08:46.416
My friend and I would like a ride.

731
01:08:47.250 --> 01:08:49.000
It wouldn't be a bother, would it?

732
01:08:49.083 --> 01:08:50.583
No, of course not.

733
01:08:53.833 --> 01:08:55.750
And thank you for helping us.

734
01:08:55.833 --> 01:08:57.083
It's my pleasure.

735
01:08:57.166 --> 01:08:58.666
Those people need you.

736
01:09:13.750 --> 01:09:17.208
Control Tower to 3-Alpha-7. Clear to start engines.

737
01:09:17.291 --> 01:09:20.916
Cuatro Vientos tower, this is 3-A-7 on Platform Alpha.

738
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:23.375
Preflight checks complete, crew on board.

739
01:09:24.708 --> 01:09:27.458
Wind 250 at six knots.

740
01:09:28.125 --> 01:09:29.583
Ready for takeoff.

741
01:09:29.666 --> 01:09:30.500
May I?

742
01:09:40.375 --> 01:09:43.791
Cleared for takeoff. We're ready.

743
01:09:58.250 --> 01:10:00.916
We have a lot of work ahead of us.

744
01:10:01.625 --> 01:10:03.333
I'm very grateful.

745
01:10:08.666 --> 01:10:10.416
What are you doing here, Lucía?

746
01:10:12.500 --> 01:10:14.375
I needed to leave the Canary Islands.

747
01:10:15.875 --> 01:10:17.208
Because of Manel?

748
01:10:20.666 --> 01:10:22.041
I think about him a lot.

749
01:10:27.375 --> 01:10:29.833
I think a lot about the night he died.

750
01:10:35.291 --> 01:10:38.708
You didn't leave his side for one minute.

751
01:10:38.791 --> 01:10:42.291
It wasn't your fault he got pneumonia.

752
01:10:42.375 --> 01:10:46.291
It wasn't your fault that antibiotics ran out on the island.

753
01:10:49.375 --> 01:10:53.083
Please, concentrate on continuing to help people.

754
01:10:56.875 --> 01:10:58.291
And you're not helping?

755
01:10:58.375 --> 01:11:02.875
You and I are on very different teams now.

756
01:11:10.083 --> 01:11:11.916
He was very grateful to you.

757
01:11:13.125 --> 01:11:14.916
He trusted you a lot.

758
01:11:17.541 --> 01:11:19.791
I know that when the time comes,

759
01:11:19.875 --> 01:11:22.333
you will do the right thing.

760
01:11:35.708 --> 01:11:37.666
Comillas! Is that your neighborhood?

761
01:11:43.166 --> 01:11:45.041
My mother and sister died there.

762
01:11:46.666 --> 01:11:47.958
I made it out.

763
01:11:52.125 --> 01:11:55.500
They would be very proud to see what you've become.

764
01:12:06.458 --> 01:12:10.958
Your daughter would be very proud of you, too, Captain.

765
01:12:27.500 --> 01:12:29.375
It's the animals from the zoo.

766
01:12:49.958 --> 01:12:51.083
We're here.

767
01:13:08.625 --> 01:13:10.791
The noise is attracting them.

768
01:13:22.333 --> 01:13:23.458
Lower it down.

769
01:13:37.375 --> 01:13:38.250
Thank you.

770
01:13:52.500 --> 01:13:53.708
See you.

771
01:14:28.583 --> 01:14:29.708
Last one!

772
01:15:02.333 --> 01:15:03.333
We're ready!

773
01:15:03.416 --> 01:15:04.541
Ready!

774
01:15:08.125 --> 01:15:09.250
No, wait!

775
01:15:12.250 --> 01:15:13.500
I'm going with them!

776
01:15:15.666 --> 01:15:17.041
What?

777
01:15:19.541 --> 01:15:20.541
Wait.

778
01:15:25.333 --> 01:15:26.416
Thank you, Prit.

779
01:15:28.250 --> 01:15:30.750
Do you realize what you're doing?

780
01:15:30.833 --> 01:15:33.416
Those people won't save you! You're Román's son!

781
01:15:34.125 --> 01:15:35.708
I can't abandon my fellow soldiers.

782
01:15:37.541 --> 01:15:38.916
I'm not like that.

783
01:15:51.291 --> 01:15:53.458
Right now there are 40 of us.

784
01:15:53.541 --> 01:15:57.166
We were going to bring in more survivors, but security is about to fall.

785
01:15:57.791 --> 01:16:00.416
We reinforced the barrier as much as we could,

786
01:16:00.500 --> 01:16:02.333
but we won't last much longer.

787
01:16:02.416 --> 01:16:04.583
From here on in, we have it covered.

788
01:16:04.666 --> 01:16:06.250
You're not alone anymore.

789
01:16:20.750 --> 01:16:22.875
There's a group trying to contain them.

790
01:16:23.375 --> 01:16:25.458
But without firepower, it's impossible.

791
01:16:25.541 --> 01:16:27.416
We can barely fend off the attacks.

792
01:16:30.541 --> 01:16:31.916
Here are the weaker ones.

793
01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:33.500
- Lucía! - On it.

794
01:16:33.583 --> 01:16:35.666
Open the gates! We're coming in!

795
01:16:56.500 --> 01:16:58.250
It's impossible to hold on.

796
01:16:58.333 --> 01:17:00.291
It's all about to go to hell.

797
01:17:01.583 --> 01:17:03.208
We need to shoot from above!

798
01:17:03.291 --> 01:17:04.958
There's access over there!

799
01:17:05.041 --> 01:17:06.958
- Guzmán! - On it!

800
01:17:08.541 --> 01:17:10.333
We need to relieve the pressure.

801
01:17:10.416 --> 01:17:11.875
Notary!

802
01:17:11.958 --> 01:17:14.291
Get out of there, folks, let's go.

803
01:17:14.375 --> 01:17:16.250
Ready? Fire!

804
01:17:34.458 --> 01:17:37.458
We're fucked! Half the city is here!

805
01:17:39.083 --> 01:17:40.708
- Save ammunition. - Damn.

806
01:17:48.750 --> 01:17:50.333
We need a plan.

807
01:17:53.375 --> 01:17:54.750
You're in charge.

808
01:17:55.791 --> 01:17:57.125
Reinforce the door!

809
01:18:02.583 --> 01:18:03.416
Roberto!

810
01:18:03.500 --> 01:18:05.041
- Cover me! - Hurry!

811
01:18:10.291 --> 01:18:12.041
- Come on! - Go!

812
01:18:14.166 --> 01:18:15.208
Shit! Come on!

813
01:18:16.458 --> 01:18:17.333
Roberto!

814
01:18:26.833 --> 01:18:27.708
Now.

815
01:18:27.791 --> 01:18:29.250
Come on! Harder!

816
01:18:44.041 --> 01:18:46.250
Listen! Listen up!

817
01:18:47.041 --> 01:18:50.541
We need to isolate them and create a containment area back there.

818
01:18:50.625 --> 01:18:52.666
Can we close off access to the ring?

819
01:18:52.750 --> 01:18:53.791
- The vomitorium? - Yes.

820
01:18:53.875 --> 01:18:55.791
We were doing that when this started.

821
01:18:55.875 --> 01:18:57.583
- We have to do it now. - Okay.

822
01:19:00.750 --> 01:19:02.208
They're coming!

823
01:19:02.291 --> 01:19:03.916
- Come on! - Come on, hurry!

824
01:19:05.250 --> 01:19:07.125
Away from the doors, quickly.

825
01:19:13.833 --> 01:19:16.333
Attention. We're going to open the gates

826
01:19:16.416 --> 01:19:18.791
to blockade the entrance with a mobile barrier.

827
01:19:18.875 --> 01:19:21.916
We'll herd the ones that get in toward the funnel and open fire.

828
01:19:23.250 --> 01:19:25.791
Pottymouth, you'll provide cover from the fence.

829
01:19:25.875 --> 01:19:27.041
Ready.

830
01:19:28.750 --> 01:19:31.250
Core, you'll guide the infected toward us.

831
01:19:31.333 --> 01:19:32.166
Ready.

832
01:19:33.833 --> 01:19:35.333
Opera? Notary?

833
01:19:35.416 --> 01:19:36.375
- Ready. - Ready.

834
01:19:37.958 --> 01:19:39.083
Status report.

835
01:19:39.166 --> 01:19:40.833
We're almost there. Not much left.

836
01:19:40.916 --> 01:19:42.250
I'll adjust this and I'm done.

837
01:19:46.458 --> 01:19:47.291
Ready!

838
01:19:47.375 --> 01:19:48.916
- Come on! - Come on, let's go!

839
01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:50.833
- Let's go! - Comillas!

840
01:19:56.458 --> 01:19:57.541
Ready?

841
01:19:59.250 --> 01:20:00.083
Come on. Here.

842
01:20:01.791 --> 01:20:02.666
Let's go!

843
01:20:06.333 --> 01:20:08.625
Okay. Be good, okay?

844
01:20:09.416 --> 01:20:11.625
Let's go. Come on.

845
01:20:12.083 --> 01:20:13.166
Come on.

846
01:20:13.750 --> 01:20:14.791
Let's go.

847
01:20:22.416 --> 01:20:23.750
Keep it up!

848
01:20:28.958 --> 01:20:30.583
Now!

849
01:21:03.791 --> 01:21:04.833
Ready?

850
01:21:58.750 --> 01:21:59.833
No, keep going!

851
01:22:00.333 --> 01:22:02.041
Come on.

852
01:22:14.958 --> 01:22:16.500
Marina! Fall back, with me!

853
01:22:27.208 --> 01:22:28.375
Come on. Push.

854
01:22:28.458 --> 01:22:29.375
Go!

855
01:22:29.458 --> 01:22:30.625
- Push there. - Come on!

856
01:22:33.500 --> 01:22:35.208
- Come on! - Push!

857
01:22:35.291 --> 01:22:37.000
Push! Keep going!

858
01:22:38.500 --> 01:22:39.791
Push! Keep it up.

859
01:23:09.708 --> 01:23:11.333
Shit, goddamn it.

860
01:23:11.833 --> 01:23:12.958
Motherfucker.

861
01:23:16.958 --> 01:23:18.625
Look out!

862
01:23:49.291 --> 01:23:50.500
- Secure it! - Hold on!

863
01:23:51.625 --> 01:23:52.750
Hold on!

864
01:23:52.833 --> 01:23:54.166
I'll help you.

865
01:23:54.250 --> 01:23:55.375
Let's go.

866
01:23:57.458 --> 01:23:58.583
Come on, get back.

867
01:24:04.958 --> 01:24:08.541
This is Opera! We need help!

868
01:24:09.375 --> 01:24:10.750
Help, please!

869
01:24:25.041 --> 01:24:26.958
Go before I bite you.

870
01:24:27.041 --> 01:24:28.375
Take this.

871
01:24:28.958 --> 01:24:29.916
Let's go!

872
01:25:05.416 --> 01:25:06.583
Out of ammo!

873
01:25:11.541 --> 01:25:12.916
We don't have any ammunition!

874
01:25:16.750 --> 01:25:18.375
They're going to enter the ring.

875
01:25:35.333 --> 01:25:36.625
I'm going to jump.

876
01:25:36.708 --> 01:25:38.833
I need you to close the doors as I go through.

877
01:25:39.833 --> 01:25:41.958
No! Roberto!

878
01:25:48.375 --> 01:25:49.458
Quickly, the doors!

879
01:26:10.875 --> 01:26:12.791
Hey! Here!

880
01:26:24.000 --> 01:26:24.875
Go! Go! Go!

881
01:26:27.875 --> 01:26:29.041
It's not working!

882
01:27:41.000 --> 01:27:42.083
Get up here!

883
01:27:57.250 --> 01:27:58.958
Are you crazy? Get out of here.

884
01:27:59.041 --> 01:28:00.458
I'm not leaving you here alone!

885
01:29:25.708 --> 01:29:29.208
This is a message to everyone still fighting out there.

886
01:29:30.791 --> 01:29:34.416
My name is Rocío Castro, I am a captain in the Spanish Army.

887
01:29:35.750 --> 01:29:38.166
Our squadron is protecting a group of heroes

888
01:29:38.250 --> 01:29:40.958
who have built a refuge at the bullring.

889
01:29:42.166 --> 01:29:45.875
We've cleared the area, raised defenses and gathered supplies.

890
01:29:47.541 --> 01:29:49.916
Anyone who wishes to can access it

891
01:29:50.000 --> 01:29:53.083
from passageways we are installing in the surrounding streets.

892
01:29:54.791 --> 01:29:58.958
If you are tired, alone or simply without hope,

893
01:29:59.041 --> 01:30:00.500
let us help you.

894
01:30:01.708 --> 01:30:05.041
All those who were unable to reach the Canary Islands at the time

895
01:30:05.708 --> 01:30:08.125
will find a home here.

896
01:30:08.750 --> 01:30:10.375
We will give you shelter.

897
01:30:11.291 --> 01:30:12.833
Whoever you are,

898
01:30:12.916 --> 01:30:14.625
wherever you come from,

899
01:30:14.708 --> 01:30:16.958
here you will be welcome.

900
01:30:18.125 --> 01:30:19.541
Good night, Madrid.

901
01:30:29.541 --> 01:30:31.958
BASED ON THE APOCALIPSIS Z BOOK SERIES BY MANEL LOUREIRO
